//! `query-via-report` documents a declaration with its `doc` attribute.
//!
//! The attribute stores its text beside the declaration verdict. The source
//! needs no doc comment.
//!
//! The checker reads the attribute into the declaration report. A query reads
//! that report with the verdict. The attribute follows `#[doc]` of Rust (The
//! Rust Reference, § Attributes).
//!
//! - see: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/

// A greeting, its documentation given by the attribute alone.
@[doc("Returns a fixed greeting.")]
def greet = "hello";
